course: dictionary
lesson: 8212
title: Retriever: a dog that brings things back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Read «retrievers that bring back birds from water». The clue is bring back: a retriever gets something and returns it to you. In your own words, a retriever is a dog that brings things back.
explain: Now read «retrievers carry back shot birds gently in soft mouths.» Gently and soft mouths tell you the dog is careful, so it does not hurt the bird it carries. The context teaches you what the word means and what kind of dog it is.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "a dog that brings things back" in place of retrievers, and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you your meaning is right.
fact: A retriever is a kind of dog bred to fetch and bring back birds that hunters have shot.
fact: Golden retrievers and Labrador retrievers are popular, friendly family dogs.
fact: Some retrievers work as guide dogs and assistance dogs, helping people in everyday life.
fact: In computing, a retriever is a program that fetches information.
fact: Retriever sounds like retrieve, which means to fetch something back.
exercise: «Retrievers carry back shot birds gently in soft mouths.» What does a retriever do? | *It fetches and brings things back | It chases its own tail | It digs holes in the garden | It herds sheep across the hills
exercise: Which of these is a retriever? | A greyhound built to sprint | A dog that herds sheep | *A golden retriever, a friendly family dog | A terrier that digs after rats
exercise: In computing, what is a retriever? | A game played with a ball | *A program that fetches information | A kind of keyboard | A type of printer paper
test: Ravi reads «retrievers that bring back birds from water». What does bring back tell him? | A retriever only eats fish | A retriever swims away forever | A retriever sleeps all day | *A retriever gets something and returns it
test: Ella has a new word and wants to check her meaning. What should she do? | Skip the sentence completely | *Swap her meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Ask if the word is a dog name | Read the word alone and guess again
exam: What is one reason golden retrievers are popular? | They only live in the sea | They can read books aloud | *They are friendly and popular family dogs | They never wag their tails
